{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T00:06:17.562586Z","id":"5633d1c64a04e668e7afa15aa3fccad637d1d970cf4072689a4f8588e2713133","body":{"detail":"bazelisk test //web:bundle_size measured gallery 32074 and extWorker 25146 after merging the local-trust, remote-instance, web and core fixes onto remote-instances. Each branch alone was within budget (the web branch measured gallery 31615, worker 24992); the merged gallery carries web/shell/src/owner-proof.ts (proofFetch on every request, the shell's half of the cookie-plus-proof session in crates/clax-http/src/local_trust.rs) beside the question-card and inbox fixes. The worker was trimmed first: stream-hub.ts now imports only web/shell/src/owner-proof-wire.ts (no imports of its own), and the composer's pairing wording comes from the native host's message (crates/clax-commands/src/commands/native_host.rs refused_confirmation), not a second copy in web/extension/src/sw/picks.ts. Options: keep the raise; or cut the gallery's proof wrapper to a fetch hook in web/shell/src/api.ts alone (requests made outside api.ts would then go unproven). Recommendation: keep it; the proof is a security fix every page needs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":16},"content_hash":"fe17b91c663320878a0dd97ba6de5d07e3259b4cabe1e4611bd80945f56c37a9"},"summary":"The gallery and extWorker budgets were raised by hand for the owner browser session's proof (gallery 31744 to 32256, extWorker 25088 to 25216)","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T01:09:45.052193Z","id":"ff3a232ae6eb6c1f411ae4a8f40e53a4c8df0f61c30bc92513b59c061f47a4e3","body":{"detail":"Measured by bazelisk test //web:bundle_size: questions 17461 before a question card had Retry, 17756 with Retry inline in web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte (git:a1226711f), 18262 once ThreadCard and QuestionCard share web/shell/src/ui/retry-link.svelte.ts and web/shell/src/ui/RetryButton.svelte, which also show why a Retry failed (git:635e53691). The shared code joins the chunk Markdown.svelte shares with the thread card; web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs counts that chunk whole on the gallery path (gallery 18262, artifact path about 300 less). Options: keep 18300; or trim to about 17800 by inlining the Retry in each card again (the two can then drift, as they had) and dropping the failure line; or lower the budget only after the question module sheds weight elsewhere. cb720cef records the budget's earlier 17500, above the spec's 16384.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":6},"end":{"line":6},"content_hash":"41fa16afd214dd3ebbd46c87ba1b0798cc15f272a699ac538bba5ef26fcdcc86"},"summary":"The question module's budget was raised by hand from 17500 to 18300 gzip bytes for the cards' shared Retry","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T01:14:19.838649Z","id":"1733e3267465290045d74d2cde5c0f0a403f5ea27f5fbfbd55af658ab4e17b6d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ff3a232ae6eb6c1f411ae4a8f40e53a4c8df0f61c30bc92513b59c061f47a4e3","summary":"Now 17900, not 18300: since git:8043a8d44 the Retry request and its failure text are web/shell/src/ui/retry-request.ts (retryCopies), which ThreadCard and QuestionCard load with a dynamic import on the first press, each card keeping its own button, failure span and CSS; RetryButton.svelte and retry-link.svelte.ts are gone. bazelisk test //web:bundle_size measures questions 17896 (17461 before a question card had Retry). The decision left is whether 17900 (439 bytes over the earlier 17500) stands, or the failure line is dropped to save some of it.","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
